            <ArticleTitle>Relvar Ellipta for asthma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>93-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/dtb.2014.8.0273</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>▼Relvar Ellipta (GSK) is a dry powder inhaler that contains a corticosteroid (fluticasone furoate) and a long-acting beta2 agonist (vilanterol trifenatate). It is licensed for once-daily use as maintenance therapy for chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) and asthma. In a previous article we considered its use in the management of COPD.1 Here we review the evidence for Relvar Ellipta in the treatment of patients with asthma.</AbstractText>
